body: "The `release` job of the Daily Release workflow failed.\n\n- Failing job: `release`\n- Run URL: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-beads/actions/runs/40177026612\n- Commit: 03e5bd8006b3ad70d008d36277be6a37f4173196\n- Date (UTC): 2026-10-25T09:36:21Z\n\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (2)\n\n> **@coderabbitai[bot]** (2026-10-25T09:37:22Z)\n>\n> <!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n> \n> <!-- This is an auto-generated issue plan by CodeRabbit -->\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⚠️ Possible Duplicate Issue(s)</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> \n> - https://github.com/unbraind/pm-beads/issues/162\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary>📝 Issue Planner</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> \n> <sub>Check the box below or use the `@coderabbitai plan` command to generate an implementation plan and prompts that you can use with your favorite coding assistant.</sub>\n> \n> - [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"8d4f2b9c-3e1a-4f7c-a9b2-d5e8f1c4a7b9\"} --> Create Plan\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary> 🧪 Issue enrichment is currently in open beta.</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> \n> \n> You can configure auto-planning by selecting labels in the issue_enrichment configuration.\n> \n> To disable automatic issue enrichment, add the following to your `.coderabbit.yaml`:\n> ```yaml\n> issue_enrichment:\n>   auto_enrich:\n>     enabled: false\n> ```\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> 💬 Have feedback or questions? Drop into our [discord](https://discord.gg/coderabbit)!\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-25T23:08:37Z)\n>\n> Recovered: the 2026-10-25 run failed only at \"Merge release metadata through protected PR\". The release PR's required checks were still queued when the 30-minute merge wait expired, because the runner pool was saturated; no check failed. The run was re-run (or, where main had advanced, dispatched fresh), and v2026.10.25 is published: npm `pm-beads@2026.10.25` and GitHub Release v2026.10.25 (2026-10-25T10:20:13Z). Future runs that fail this way are recovered automatically by the host-side release re-run sweep (unbraind/pm-cli-companion#273)."
